I stand by the chilled case in the supermarket.
I see a small foil tray.
I pick the tray up.
What is inside it?
A man reaches past me.
He also takes a tray.
"Excuse me," I say to the man.
"What is this?"
"It is leverpostej," he says.
"You put it on rye bread."
"It is good!"
I am curious.
I would like to try it.
Maybe I will like it.
I would like to taste it.
